course: dictionary
lesson: 3434
title: Words for faces
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your eyebrows are the two lines of short hair above your eyes. Eyebrow is a noun, and you can have one eyebrow or two eyebrows. «Gran hands Sam a present, Mum raises an eyebrow and says "What do you say?"» Mum does not say anything rude, but one raised eyebrow tells Sam she is waiting for a polite answer.
explain: Writers use eyebrows to show feelings, because readers can picture a face. Raised eyebrows mean surprise. A frown means crossed or angry. Knitted eyebrows, pulled together, show someone is worried or thinking hard.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In «Mum raises an eyebrow», the word tells you she is showing doubt with one small movement. Context helps you see that a face can say a lot without any words.
fact: An eyebrow is the line of short hair above your eye.
fact: «Raise an eyebrow» means to show surprise or doubt by moving your eyebrows up.
fact: Eyebrows help keep sweat and rain from running into your eyes.
fact: «Knitted eyebrows» means eyebrows pulled together, often when someone is worried or thinking hard.
fact: A helmet should sit level, about two fingers' width above the eyebrows, with the strap buckled.
exercise: What is an eyebrow? | The part of your ear you hear with | The skin on your chin | The bone in your nose | *The line of short hair above your eye
exercise: «Mum raises an eyebrow and says "What do you say?"» What does raising an eyebrow show? | *Surprise or doubt | Feeling cold | Being happy about a present | Being very tired and sleepy
exercise: Which phrase shows someone is worried or thinking hard? | Bare forehead | Bushy eyebrows | *Knitted eyebrows | Raised eyebrows
test: Eyebrows help keep what out of your eyes? | Dust from the floor only | Noise | *Sweat and rain | Sunlight
test: In a story, a character with a frown is most likely feeling what? | Hungry | *Cross or angry | Sleepy after a long night | Very tall
exam: In the sentence «A helmet should sit level, about two fingers above the eyebrows», what does the word eyebrows tell you about where the helmet goes? | It sits behind the ears | It sits in the hand | It sits on the chin | *It sits just above the eyebrows, on the forehead
